---
import QuestionLayout from '@layouts/QuestionLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [{
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'How do I run the agent-blocked weekly demo?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Read the public blog write-up for the deny story (agent proposes; runtime decides). The runnable weekly-demos folder is not publicly cloneable yet — tracked in traverse-framework/.github#30. Do not invent a local path or assume git clone works.',
    },
  }],
});

const relatedLinks = [
  { href: '/blog/agent-freestyle-blocked.html', label: 'Agent freestyle → blocked (blog)' },
  { href: '/blog/same-wasm-multi-host.html', label: 'Same WASM multi-host (blog)' },
  { href: '/what-is-real-today.html', label: 'What is real today' },
  { href: '/questions/what-does-discover-execute-trace-mean.html', label: 'discover → execute → trace' },
  { href: '/questions/how-does-traverse-prevent-ai-agent-errors.html', label: 'How does Traverse prevent AI agent errors?' },
  { href: '/questions/what-is-a-trace-artifact.html', label: 'What is a trace artifact?' },
  { href: '/agents.html', label: 'For AI agents' },
];
---
<QuestionLayout
  title="How do I run the agent-blocked weekly demo?"
  description="Public path today: read the deny-demo blog. The weekly-demos runnable repo is not public yet (.github#30). Agent proposes; runtime decides."
  canonical="https://traverse-framework.com/questions/how-do-i-run-the-agent-blocked-weekly-demo.html"
  category="Getting started"
  relatedLinks={relatedLinks}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p>The project direction in one scene: an agent freestyles a large wire; <code>core.authorize@1.2.0</code> denies; you get a trace. <strong>Discover → execute → trace.</strong> The agent proposes; the runtime decides.</p>

  <h2>What you can run today (public)</h2>
  <p>Start with the write-up — that is the citeable public surface:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/blog/agent-freestyle-blocked.html">The agent freestyled a $2.4M wire. The runtime said no.</a></li>
    <li>Follow-up multi-host scene: <a href="/blog/same-wasm-multi-host.html">Same WASM. Browser and Node match. Agent still can’t freestyle.</a></li>
    <li>Citeable snapshot: <a href="/what-is-real-today.html">What is real today</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Runnable repo status</h2>
  <p>The shared monorepo <code>traverse-framework/weekly-demos</code> holds dated runnable folders for maintainers, but it is <strong>not publicly cloneable yet</strong> (unauthenticated API returns 404). Do <strong>not</strong> follow old <code>git clone https://github.com/traverse-framework/weekly-demos.git</code> instructions — they hit a closed door. Visibility vs public docs is tracked in <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/.github/issues/30" target="_blank" rel="noopener">.github#30</a>. No public zip/mirror is published from this page; we will not invent one.</p>

  <h2>What you should take away</h2>
  <p>Freestyle prose is not authority. A governed capability under discover → execute → trace is. When the runnable repo is public (or a published artifact replaces it), this page will say so explicitly.</p>
</QuestionLayout>
